# Keep the build context tight. The Dockerfile selectively COPYs what it needs;
# this just reduces the context Docker sends to the daemon.

# Build outputs
**/target
**/*.bak

# VCS / editor
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Dev-only docs / tooling — not in the runtime image. tools/camera-simctl is
# a workspace member, so cargo needs to see its Cargo.toml to evaluate the
# workspace at all; let it through and let the Dockerfile decide what to COPY.
docs
tools
!tools/camera-simctl
DESIGN.md
README.md
LICENSE*
*.md

# Tests don't go into release artifacts
**/tests

# CI lives outside the build context
.woodpecker.yml
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
